From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:43:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: mediatek: mt6789: guard the sleep PM ops

Reference the paris sleep PM ops through pm_sleep_ptr(), as the other
MediaTek paris drivers do, so a kernel without CONFIG_PM_SLEEP drops
them. With PM_SLEEP=y, as on the Q25, the pointer is unchanged.

The Q25's 7.0.0-q25-cfi-test kernels were built from a tree carrying
this change.
---
 drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mt6789.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mt6789.c b/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mt6789.c
index b71f6b48..b4c58209 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mt6789.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mt6789.c
@@ -1262,7 +1262,7 @@ static struct platform_driver mt6789_pinctrl_driver = {
 	.driver = {
 		.name = "mt6789-pinctrl",
 		.of_match_table = mt6789_pinctrl_of_match,
-		.pm = &mtk_paris_pinctrl_pm_ops,
+		.pm = pm_sleep_ptr(&mtk_paris_pinctrl_pm_ops),
 	},
 	.probe = mtk_paris_pinctrl_probe,
 };
